==Battleground==
*1 [[Axoloty]] spawns as the boss after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Zamelle]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Deathkory]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[Red Cyclone]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
Due to the stage design here, each of the enemies can be fought alone, and all of them are relatively easy to handle. The important thing is to damage the base little by little, not allowing an enemy to spawn until the previous one is gone. [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] are excellent here as he can tanks every attacks regardless of strong the attack are such as Axoloty whose attack normally one-shot everything. Obviously you should spawn him early since Axoloty might one-shot your base before your Metal Cat stop them. Even then, you won't really need him as this stage isn't hard at all.

Axoloty is only ever a threat when supporting other units, so anything capable of breaking that barrier can handle that phase easily, just make sure you spawn a unit before Axoloty hits your base to avoid dying instantly. Due to Axoloty's ridiculously long backswing, you can also use this phase to max out your money.

Zamelle can be handled with [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]], though other anti-Zombies can work. Zamelle can cause problems if given the chance to revive while Deathkory is out, so Zombie Killer is important here.

Deathkory can be easily handled by wave-immune Cats and timing any Shield Piercer between wave attacks. Wave blockers also work wonders here.

This stage ends with Red Cyclone, whose low range and pair of traits keep it from being a threat. [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] and [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] should be more than enough while generalist attackers defeat it.

